# wat core

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for architecture, build commands, and repo rules.

## Layout

- `cmd/wat` — CLI; depends on `agenthooks`
- `agenthooks` — unified hook library (stdlib only)
- `claudehook`, `copilothook`, `cursorhook` — independent per-agent SDKs
- `plan/` — local-only design docs (gitignored); do not commit
- `docs/` — committed user-facing reference (agent formats, doc index)

## Layering

- Do not add the old `internal/core` + host-package layout unless a task requires it.
- Keep per-agent SDKs usable without `agenthooks`.
- New exported API must include godoc comments (enforced by revive in CI).

## Version pinning

Pin **exact versions** for tools and actions referenced in repo config and docs. Do not use `@latest`, `version: latest`, or floating major/minor tags (e.g. `@v4`, `@v6`) in:

- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (exact action release tags, e.g. `actions/checkout@v4.3.1`, `golangci-lint-action@v6.5.2`; tool versions, e.g. `golangci-lint@v1.64.8`, `govulncheck@v1.6.0`)
- `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and install instructions

When bumping a pinned version, update every reference in the same change.

**Audit:** After workflow edits, run `rg 'uses:\s*[\w./-]+@v\d+$' .github/workflows` — zero matches required. See `.cursor/skills/ci-pins/SKILL.md`.

